<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/064R">Example <span data-tag="064R">9.2.5.16</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category which is sequentially cocomplete. Then an object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $(\aleph _0, \aleph _1)$-compact if and only if the corepresentable functor $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( C, \bullet )$ commutes with sequential colimits. See Corollary <a data-tag="06EB" href="/tag/06EB">9.2.3.8</a>. </p>
